window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-f7652a24ac1e64cf"]={"key":"ny_main-f7652a24ac1e64cf","group":"ny_main","uid":"f7652a24ac1e64cf","rank":18,"title":"netherfield case review revision copy 01","occupation":"audio_video_technicians","archetype":"supplied_source","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are the Audio and Video Technician at Netherfield Authority. In the week before Gildenhall Council’s 19 August 2042 publication meeting, Viktor Schuyler needs a revised case-review video that Leonie Vasquez can use to brief frontline staff and execute the documented editorial changes. The supplied case material has been through an untidy handoff: repeated records and labels that do not always agree are present, so the finished asset must preserve what the records actually support rather than quietly choosing a winner. Work from `case_review_draft.docx` and `review_comments.xlsx`, then produce `gildenhall_case_review_revised.docx` in the top level of the working directory you start in, using exactly that filename. Treat Leonie’s review comments as the authorized change request: apply the requested cuts, ordering, pacing, and transitions, but do not make up connective narration, case facts, dates, outcomes, or participants. Keep any material conflict visible and explain its treatment in the embedded change log rather than converting it into an unsupported statement. The document should function as the revised timed case-review video asset for an editor and a frontline briefing: show a coherent sequence, readable segment or shot timing, clear transitions, and enough editorial detail that the authorized changes can be executed without reopening the source. Embed a change log in the same document that identifies every review comment, its disposition, the affected segment or time range, and the resulting change; record anything not changed or still needing confirmation. Use source wording for facts unless a comment explicitly authorizes an edit, and do not carry source-only working material into the finished asset. Keep the document concise enough to use during the briefing, make the timeline internally consistent, and ensure the finished file is clean, legible, and free of unexplained placeholders.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/case_review_draft.docx` — The current timed case-review draft, including the source case facts, segment content, timing information, and existing editorial structure.\n- `references/review_comments.xlsx` — Leonie Vasquez's review comments and the accompanying case-record material needed to identify the authorized editorial changes and preserve source-supported facts.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `gildenhall_case_review_revised.docx` — A revised timed case-review video production document representing the edited asset, with the revised sequence and an embedded change log. (Write the file into the top level of the solver's starting working directory.; Use exactly the specified filename.; Include the revised timed sequence and the embedded change log in the same document.; Preserve source-supported facts and distinguish unresolved conflicts from confirmed content.; Do not add unsupported narration, facts, participants, outcomes, or source-only working fields.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/case_review_draft.docx","bytes":40041,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/836913386ccb169d314d3ee0a59b7408a141b3752aa0890051cc80397dc51855.docx","sha256":"836913386ccb169d314d3ee0a59b7408a141b3752aa0890051cc80397dc51855","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Gildenhall Council Case Review - Current Timed Draft\nNetherfield Authority | Frontline briefing assembly | Review copy\nAsset\nCase review timed assembly\nPrepared for\nGildenhall Council frontline briefing\nReview owner\nLeonie Vasquez\nAuthorization\nViktor Schuyler\n\nCurrent assembly. The wording in the sequence is the working source wording; the transition column records the present cut.\nOrder\nShot ID\nCase ref\nIn\nOut\nDuration\n(s)\nPicture / source wording\nCurrent transition / edit note\n1\nOPN-A\n-\n00:00.00\n00:10.00\n10.00\nGildenhall Council case review. Frontline briefing.\nOpen on title card; 1.50 s dissolve to OPN-B.\n2\nOPN-B\n-\n00:10.00\n00:18.00\n8.00\nGildenhall Council case review. Frontline briefing.\n1.50 s dissolve to CAS-7714.\n3\nCAS-7714\nGH-7714\n00:18.00\n00:58.00\n40.00\nAccess route request. The access request was logged after a blocked side entrance was reported. The field visit recorded the side entrance clear at close of inspection. Status: Closed - evidence recorded. Event date/time: 2042-08-06 09:15.\nStraight cut to BRG-01.\n4\nBRG-01\n-\n00:58.00\n01:02.00\n4.00\nSilent bridge; no new spoken words.\nStraight cut to CAS-8842-A.\n5\nCAS-8842-A\nGH-8842\n01:02.00\n02:30.00\n88.00\nDraft label: Resident liaison query. The resident asked for a review of the permit decision. The file contains the submitted permit copy and the response note. Status: Review pending. Event date/time: 07/08/2042 14:30.\nStraight cut to CAS-8842-B.\n6\nCAS-8842-B\nGH-8842\n02:30.00\n02:42.00\n12.00\nDraft label: Resident liaison query. The resident asked for a review of the permit decision. The file contains the submitted permit copy and the response note. Status: Review pending. Event date/time: 07/08/2042 14:30.\nStraight cut to CAS-9061.\n7\nCAS-9061\nGH-9061\n02:42.00\n03:28.00\n46.00\nWelfare contact follow-up. A follow-up call was logged after the initial welfare contact. The contact record includes a callback time and a named service inbox. Status: Follow-up recorded. Event date/time: 2042-08-07 10:05.\n2.00 s dissolve to CAS-9428.\n8\nCAS-9428\nGH-9428\n03:28.00\n04:24.00\n56.00\nAccommodation inspection. The inspection record notes a missing handrail on the upper landing. A repair request was attached to the record. Status: Repair request attached. Event date/time: 2042-08-08 16:20.\nFade out to END-A.\n9\nEND-A\n-\n04:24.00\n04:40.00\n16.00\nCase review. Source wording retained.\nFade out.\nRuntime of current assembly: 04:40.00","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/review_comments.xlsx","bytes":7763,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/91bc248d3ac4d99fc2b0d80f115fea5c37a8b0551091a01f973ede8cfc13e4b0.xlsx","sha256":"91bc248d3ac4d99fc2b0d80f115fea5c37a8b0551091a01f973ede8cfc13e4b0","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Review export","row_count":24,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Leonie Vasquez - Editorial review comments"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Netherfield Authority / Gildenhall Council case review"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Review pass 2 - comment export with register extract"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Comment ID","Reviewer","Area","Comment","Authorized edit"]},{"r":"6","cells":["CMT-01","Leonie Vasquez","Opening / OPN-B","Remove OPN-B. Keep the first opening card only, and shorten its title hold so the briefing does not begin with the same card twice.","OPN-A = 8.00 s; omit OPN-B (00:10.00-00:18.00)."]},{"r":"7","cells":["CMT-02","Leonie Vasquez","GH-8842 / CAS-8842-B","Remove the second GH-8842 occurrence. It is not a separate case segment.","Omit CAS-8842-B (02:30.00-02:42.00); retain CAS-8842-A."]},{"r":"8","cells":["CMT-03","Leonie Vasquez","Sequence","After the bridge from GH-7714, place CAS-9061 before CAS-8842-A.","Order: OPN-A > CAS-7714 > BRG-01 > CAS-9061 > CAS-8842-A > CAS-9428 > END-A; reflow continuously from 00:00.00; retain the bridge straight cut into CAS-9061."]},{"r":"9","cells":["CMT-04","Leonie Vasquez","Bridge / BRG-01","Shorten the silent bridge pause, but retain a readable beat before the moved case.","BRG-01 = 2.00 s."]},{"r":"10","cells":["CMT-05","Leonie Vasquez","GH-9428 / CAS-9428","Trim the long still-frame hold in CAS-9428; retain the source wording and evidence.","CAS-9428 = 32.00 s."]},{"r":"11","cells":["CMT-06","Leonie Vasquez","OPN-A -> CAS-7714","At the retained opening-to-first-case boundary, replace the slow dissolve with a hard picture cut and short audio carry.","OPN-A -> CAS-7714: hard cut; audio carry 0.50 s."]},{"r":"12","cells":["CMT-07","Leonie Vasquez","CAS-9061 -> CAS-8842-A","At the new CAS-9061 to CAS-8842-A boundary, use a brief dip to black.","CAS-9061 -> CAS-8842-A: dip to black 1.00 s."]},{"r":"13","cells":["CMT-08","Leonie Vasquez","CAS-8842-A -> CAS-9428","Keep the existing dissolve into CAS-9428 after CAS-8842-A.","CAS-8842-A -> CAS-9428: dissolve 2.00 s."]},{"r":"14","cells":["CMT-09","Leonie Vasquez","GH-8842 labels","Do not select a canonical label for GH-8842. Keep the draft and register labels attributed to their source contexts.","On-screen locator: GH-8842; label confirmation required."]},{"r":"15","cells":["CMT-10","Leonie Vasquez","GH-8842 event date/time","Retain the literal GH-8842 event date/time. Do not infer the day/month order.","Retain the source text verbatim; date confirmation required."]},{"r":"16","cells":["CMT-11","Leonie Vasquez","END-A","Keep the closing card wording and timing unchanged.","END-A = 16.00 s; retain fade out."]},{"r":"17","cells":["CMT-12","Leonie Vasquez","All segments","Do not add connective voiceover or factual narration between segments.","Use source wording only; no new narration."]},{"r":"20","cells":["Case register extract"]},{"r":"21","cells":["Record key","Case reference","Register label","Event date/time","Event wording","Evidence / status wording","Authoritative source order","Retired helper order","Legacy QA check"]},{"r":"22","cells":["CR-7714-1","GH-7714","Access route request","2042-08-06 09:15","The access request was logged after a blocked side entrance was reported.","The field visit recorded the side entrance clear at close of inspection. Status: Closed - evidence recorded.","1","4","pass"]},{"r":"23","cells":["CR-8842-1","GH-8842","Permit review query","07/08/2042 14:30","The resident asked for a review of the permit decision.","The file contains the submitted permit copy and the response note. Status: Review pending.","2","1","=1/0  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"24","cells":["CR-8842-2","GH-8842","Permit review query","07/08/2042 14:30","The resident asked for a review of the permit decision.","The file contains the submitted permit copy and the response note. Status: Review pending.","2","1","pass"]},{"r":"25","cells":["CR-9061-1","GH-9061","Welfare contact follow-up","2042-08-07 10:05","A follow-up call was logged after the initial welfare contact.","The contact record includes a callback time and a named service inbox. Status: Follow-up recorded.","3","2","pass"]},{"r":"26","cells":["CR-9428-1","GH-9428","Accommodation inspection","2042-08-08 16:20","The inspection record notes a missing handrail on the upper landing.","A repair request was attached to the record. Status: Repair request attached.","4","3","pass"]},{"r":"28","cells":["Export retained as received."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/gildenhall_case_review_revised.docx","bytes":41865,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/c38ded9addbe253a9760b67bc70fcb4d72bf5dde10850e5e863c6f5e561f8d4f.docx","sha256":"c38ded9addbe253a9760b67bc70fcb4d72bf5dde10850e5e863c6f5e561f8d4f","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Gildenhall Council Case Review - Revised Timed Video Asset\nNetherfield Authority | Gildenhall Council frontline briefing | Executable editorial sequence\nRevision status\nAuthorized revision copy\nAuthorized change request\nLeonie Vasquez\nAuthorization\nViktor Schuyler\nFinal runtime\n03:52.00\nEDITORIAL\nCONTROL\nUse the source wording below. Do not add connective voiceover or factual narration. The slash-delimited date/time remains literal, and the conflicting source labels remain attributed pending confirmation.\nRevised Timed Sequence\n#\nTime\nShot / purpose\nSource copy / on-screen direction\nNext transition / edit\n1\n00:00.00\n00:08.00\n8.00 s\nOPN-A\nTitle card\nGildenhall Council case review. Frontline briefing.\nHard picture cut to CAS-7714; 0.50 s audio carry.\n2\n00:08.00\n00:48.00\n40.00 s\nCAS-7714\nCase segment\nGH-7714\nAccess route request. The access request was logged after a blocked side entrance was reported. The field visit recorded the side entrance clear at close of inspection. Status: Closed - evidence recorded. Event date/time: 2042-08-06 09:15.\nStraight cut to BRG-01.\n3\n00:48.00\n00:50.00\n2.00 s\nBRG-01\nSilent bridge\nSilent bridge; no new spoken words.\nStraight cut to CAS-9061.\n4\n00:50.00\n01:36.00\n46.00 s\nCAS-9061\nCase segment\nGH-9061\nWelfare contact follow-up. A follow-up call was logged after the initial welfare contact. The contact record includes a callback time and a named service inbox. Status: Follow-up recorded. Event date/time: 2042-08-07 10:05.\n1.00 s dip to black to CAS-8842-A.\n5\n01:36.00\n03:04.00\n88.00 s\nCAS-8842-A\nCase segment\nGH-8842\nDraft label: Resident liaison query. Register label: Permit review query. The resident asked for a review of the permit decision. The file contains the submitted permit copy and the response note. Status: Review pending. Event date/time: 07/08/2042 14:30.\n2.00 s dissolve to CAS-9428.\n6\n03:04.00\n03:36.00\n32.00 s\nCAS-9428\nCase segment\nGH-9428\nAccommodation inspection. The inspection record notes a missing handrail on the upper landing. A repair request was attached to the record. Status: Repair request attached. Event date/time: 2042-08-08 16:20.\nFade out to END-A.\n7\n03:36.00\n03:52.00\n16.00 s\nEND-A\nClosing card\nCase review. Source wording retained.\nFade out.\nFinal runtime: 03:52.00\nOutstanding Confirmation\nLabel treatment\nThe draft label \"Resident liaison query\" and the register label \"Permit review query\" remain attributed to their source contexts. No canonical label is selected.\nDate treatment\n\"07/08/2042 14:30\" remains literal. Confirm the calendar interpretation before any conversion or verbal expansion.\n\n\nEmbedded Change Log\nEach Leonie Vasquez review comment is mapped below to its disposition and the executable result in this revision.\nID\nReview comment / authorization\nAffected segment or time\nDisposition and resulting change\nCMT-01\nRemove OPN-B. Keep the first opening card only, and shorten its title hold so the briefing does not begin with the same card twice. Authorized: OPN-A = 8.00 s; omit OPN-B (00:10.00-00:18.00).\nOPN-A 00:00.00-00:08.00; OPN-B removed\nApplied - OPN-A is 8.00 s. OPN-B is omitted from the revised sequence.\nCMT-02\nRemove the second GH-8842 occurrence. It is not a separate case segment. Authorized: Omit CAS-8842-B (02:30.00-02:42.00); retain CAS-8842-A.\nGH-8842 / CAS-8842-A 01:36.00-03:04.00; source CAS-8842-B removed\nApplied - GH-8842 appears once as CAS-8842-A; the second source occurrence is not a case segment.\nCMT-03\nAfter the bridge from GH-7714, place CAS-9061 before CAS-8842-A. Authorized: Order: OPN-A > CAS-7714 > BRG-01 > CAS-9061 > CAS-8842-A > CAS-9428 > END-A; reflow continuously from 00:00.00; retain the bridge straight cut into CAS-9061.\nSequence rows 1-7, 00:00.00-03:52.00\nApplied - the authorized sequence order is reflowed continuously from 00:00.00, with the bridge straight cut into CAS-9061.\nCMT-04\nShorten the silent bridge pause, but retain a readable beat before the moved case. Authorized: BRG-01 = 2.00 s.\nBRG-01 00:48.00-00:50.00\nApplied - the silent bridge is 2.00 s and remains a readable beat.\nCMT-05\nTrim the long still-frame hold in CAS-9428; retain the source wording and evidence. Authorized: CAS-9428 = 32.00 s.\nGH-9428 / CAS-9428 03:04.00-03:36.00\nApplied - CAS-9428 is 32.00 s; its source wording and evidence are retained.\nCMT-06\nAt the retained opening-to-first-case boundary, replace the slow dissolve with a hard picture cut and short audio carry. Authorized: OPN-A -> CAS-7714: hard cut; audio carry 0.50 s.\nOPN-A -> CAS-7714 at 00:08.00\nApplied - hard picture cut with 0.50 s audio carry.\nCMT-07\nAt the new CAS-9061 to CAS-8842-A boundary, use a brief dip to black. Authorized: CAS-9061 -> CAS-8842-A: dip to black 1.00 s.\nCAS-9061 -> CAS-8842-A at 01:36.00\nApplied - 1.00 s dip to black at the moved case boundary.\nCMT-08\nKeep the existing dissolve into CAS-9428 after CAS-8842-A. Authorized: CAS-8842-A -> CAS-9428: dissolve 2.00 s.\nCAS-8842-A -> CAS-9428 at 03:04.00\nApplied - 2.00 s dissolve retained into CAS-9428.\nCMT-09\nDo not select a canonical label for GH-8842. Keep the draft and register labels attributed to their source contexts. Authorized: On-screen locator: GH-8842; label confirmation required.\nGH-8842 / CAS-8842-A 01:36.00-03:04.00\nApplied - on-screen locator is GH-8842; draft and register labels remain attributed. Label confirmation is required.\nCMT-10\nRetain the literal GH-8842 event date/time. Do not infer the day/month order. Authorized: Retain the source text verbatim; date confirmation required.\nGH-8842 / CAS-8842-A 01:36.00-03:04.00\nApplied - 07/08/2042 14:30 is retained literally; no day/month interpretation is made. Date confirmation is required.\nCMT-11\nKeep the closing card wording and timing unchanged. Authorized: END-A = 16.00 s; retain fade out.\nEND-A 03:36.00-03:52.00\nRetained - closing card source wording, 16.00 s duration, and fade out are unchanged.\nCMT-12\nDo not add connective voiceover or factual narration between segments. Authorized: Use source wording only; no new narration.\nAll timed segments, 00:00.00-03:52.00\nApplied - no connective voiceover or factual narration has been added between segments.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted file `gildenhall_case_review_revised.docx` is present at the required path, opens as a valid DOCX, and can be rendered without package corruption.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted file.","grader_hint":"Check the filename and top-level location, open the DOCX package, and render it with an offline office tool. This is a scaffolding item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document contains a visibly labeled embedded change-log section.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered document text.","grader_hint":"Search extracted text and the rendered document for a clear heading identifying the change log. This is a scaffolding item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delivered document clearly identifies the asset as the revised Gildenhall Council case review and makes its frontline briefing purpose apparent.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Title, opening description, and audience language in the deliverable.","grader_hint":"Confirm that a reader can identify the case-review asset, its revised status, and its intended frontline audience without consulting the references."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every distinct case reference represented in the source case records is represented in the revised timed sequence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"The two supplied reference files compared with the timed sequence in the deliverable.","grader_hint":"Extract the set of distinct case references from the source records and compare it with the set of references in the sequence, excluding mentions inside the change log."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each distinct case reference appears once in the revised timed sequence, and the repeated source occurrence is not presented as an additional case segment.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source case-reference occurrences and the deliverable's sequence table or storyboard.","grader_hint":"Count case references in the sequence itself, not in the change log. Compare the count with the distinct source-reference set rather than the raw source-row count."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The revised asset retains all material source-supported case facts needed for the briefing and does not omit a material event, status, or evidence statement.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source text and case records compared with the revised sequence.","grader_hint":"Use a fact-by-fact comparison of the source records and draft against the revised asset. Do not penalize purely editorial trimming that is explicitly authorized in the comments."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The order of the case segments and editorial beats follows the ordering changes explicitly requested in Leonie Vasquez's comments.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Authorized ordering comments in `review_comments.xlsx` and the sequence in the deliverable.","grader_hint":"For every comment that names a relative or absolute ordering change, compare the resulting sequence against that instruction. Do not infer a new order from the stale helper field."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every authorized cut, trim, pause adjustment, and transition change in the review comments is reflected in the revised timed asset.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Review comments, draft timing/content, and revised sequence.","grader_hint":"Build an action-by-action comparison from the comments. Confirm that each specified edit is visible in the revised content or timing, rather than merely described in the change log."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Facts, outcomes, dates, and participants are unchanged except where a review comment explicitly authorizes the change.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source facts, comments, and deliverable text.","grader_hint":"Compare factual statements in the output with the source corpus and authorized comments. Treat wording changes as acceptable only when they preserve meaning or are explicitly requested."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Conflicting source labels remain attributable to their source context or are otherwise made visibly unresolved; the revised asset does not silently replace them with a single unsupported label.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Inconsistent labels in the source material and their treatment in the revised asset and change log.","grader_hint":"Locate the conflicting labels in the references and inspect the corresponding output passages. Credit explicit attribution or an explicit unresolved-status treatment; do not credit silent normalization."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Date and time facts in the revised asset are copied faithfully from the source or changed only in a way expressly authorized by the comments, without silently converting a source representation into a different fact.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Date/time strings in both references and the deliverable.","grader_hint":"Compare the literal source representations and any authorized replacement with the output. Check both the narrative text and any timing metadata."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The ambiguous date representation is handled defensibly: the output does not assert an unsupported interpretation, and the uncertainty or required confirmation is visible in the change log.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Ambiguous source date, corresponding output text, and change-log entry.","grader_hint":"Identify the source date that permits more than one calendar interpretation. Credit literal preservation with a clear ambiguity note or another equally defensible treatment, and reject an unexplained choice of interpretation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every review comment in the supplied comments file has a corresponding entry in the embedded change log.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Complete comment list in `review_comments.xlsx` and the deliverable's change log.","grader_hint":"Match comments by their supplied identifier, wording, or uniquely identifying subject. Do not count a generic statement that fails to map to an individual comment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each change-log entry states a clear disposition, such as applied, retained, not changed, or needing confirmation, consistent with the resulting asset.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Embedded change log and revised asset.","grader_hint":"Inspect every mapped entry and verify that its status is explicit and not contradicted by the actual sequence or wording."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each change-log entry identifies the affected case, segment, or time range precisely enough for an editor to locate the change.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Change-log locators and the timed sequence.","grader_hint":"A locator may be a case reference, segment label, shot label, or time range, but it must resolve unambiguously to the revised asset."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every retained or revised timecode in the deliverable agrees with the source or the authorized comment within ±0.01 seconds.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source timing, authorized timing changes, and output timecodes.","grader_hint":"Parse start, end, and duration values where present and compare them with the applicable source or comment value using an absolute tolerance of 0.01 seconds."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The revised timeline is internally ordered: each segment starts no earlier than the preceding segment's end, with no unexplained overlap or gap greater than ±0.01 seconds.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered timeline or extracted timing table in the deliverable.","grader_hint":"Sort by displayed sequence order and calculate adjacent end-to-start differences. Allow a maximum rounding discrepancy of 0.01 seconds; require any larger gap or overlap to be explicitly explained."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The stated final runtime equals the end of the last timed segment, or the sum of the revised segment durations where that is the source convention, within ±0.01 seconds.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Output runtime statement and all revised segment timings.","grader_hint":"Use the convention consistently with the source draft, calculate the runtime offline, and compare with the stated value using ±0.01 seconds."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The revised pacing visibly implements the requested removal of repetition and adjustment of unnecessarily long holds without making the briefing rushed or materially less intelligible.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Draft, review comments, revised timing, and rendered deliverable.","grader_hint":"Compare the affected passages before and after revision. Credit a proportionate timing change that preserves comprehension and reject unchanged problem passages or excessive compression."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Transitions occur at the locations and in the form authorized by the comments and make the revised sequence easy to follow.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Review comments and transition annotations in the revised asset.","grader_hint":"Check each authorized transition location and type. Evaluate whether the transition connects adjacent content coherently rather than serving as decorative or unsupported material."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The revised asset contains no new connective voiceover or factual narration beyond source wording and explicitly authorized comment text.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All narrative text in the deliverable compared with the source corpus and review comments.","grader_hint":"Extract spoken-script, caption, and narration text. Every factual or connective statement must be traceable to a reference or an explicit authorized edit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The deliverable introduces no unsupported case outcome, participant, event, date, causal explanation, or visual claim.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Output claims compared with both supplied references.","grader_hint":"Review every declarative claim and named entity in the output. Credit only claims grounded in the references or directly authorized by a comment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Source wording is retained for unchanged factual passages, with edits limited to the authorized editorial changes rather than broad unrequested rewriting.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Draft text, case records, comments, and revised text.","grader_hint":"Use text comparison with allowance for formatting and explicitly requested edits. Penalize paraphrase that changes evidentiary meaning or obscures the source."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The timed asset is executable by an editor and usable by frontline staff: segment purpose, timing, content, and transition information are sufficiently clear to carry out the revision without reopening the references.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered deliverable viewed as a standalone production document.","grader_hint":"Ask whether a competent editor could implement the sequence and whether a frontline briefing user could follow it. Missing locators, vague timing, or unexplained production notation should fail this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The change log explicitly records the treatment of the material label conflict and any other source matter that remains unresolved or requires confirmation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conflict in references and corresponding change-log notes.","grader_hint":"Confirm that the log distinguishes an applied editorial change from an unresolved source issue and identifies what would need confirmation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Ordering, timing, and factual selections in the output are derived from the primary draft, case records, and authorized comments, not from the stale values in the retired helper field.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"The retired helper values in the workbook, authoritative source fields, comments, and output sequence.","grader_hint":"Compare any output ordering or timing that could have been influenced by the helper with the authoritative fields and comments. A result matching the stale helper while contradicting the authoritative material fails."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The residual source formula error is omitted from the revised asset and does not become a displayed fact, timing value, label, or change-log conclusion.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"The residual error cell in the supplied workbook and all output content.","grader_hint":"Trace output values and text back to source cells. The error must be ignored rather than copied, paraphrased, or used in a calculation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delivered DOCX contains no `#REF!`, `#DIV/0!`, `#VALUE!`, or equivalent spreadsheet error tokens.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Extracted DOCX XML text and rendered document.","grader_hint":"Search all document text, including tables, headers, footers, and embedded change-log content, for the listed error tokens. This is a hygiene item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered document has no clipped, overlapping, or unreadable timing, sequence, or change-log content.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered pages of the submitted DOCX.","grader_hint":"Inspect every page at normal reading scale. Fail for cut-off cells, text collisions, unreadable contrast, or timing information that cannot be reliably read."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"As a whole, the revised asset has coherent sequencing, proportionate pacing, and clear transitions while remaining faithful to the supplied case material.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Standalone rendered deliverable and supplied references.","grader_hint":"Make an overall professional usability judgment. A technically traceable file that reads as a disjointed, confusing, or editorially unfinished asset should not receive credit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any added scene, participant, outcome, factual narration, or connective claim that is absent from both references and not authorized by a review comment incurs a penalty of −6.","weight":-6.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All added substantive content in the deliverable compared with the supplied references and authorized comments.","grader_hint":"Apply this once if any unsupported substantive addition is found; do not apply it for ordinary formatting, labels needed to identify source material, or clearly marked editorial transition notation."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Netherfield Authority is preparing a case-review video for Gildenhall Council's frontline briefing and publication workflow. Viktor Schuyler has authorized the revision, and Leonie Vasquez needs a clean, executable editorial asset with the changes traceable.","difficulty_sources":["The case records contain a repeated record and labels that conflict across source material.","Review comments authorize a finite set of sequencing, pacing, trimming, and transition edits.","The source workbook contains mixed date representations, a stale retired helper field, and one residual formula error."],"authoring_plan":{"purpose":"Construct two text-office references whose content determines the gold revised timed case-review asset. The build agent should choose fresh synthetic literal identifiers, dates, labels, and timing values that do not reuse literal values from the task brief.","reference_files":{"case_review_draft.docx":{"semantic_content":["Create a draft case-review video production document for Netherfield Authority and Gildenhall Council.","Include a finite timed sequence of synthetic case segments, each tied to a stable case reference and supported case facts.","Include source wording for the case facts, the current sequence, existing timing, and the editorial passages that Leonie Vasquez comments on.","Include one repeated case-record occurrence in the draft/source material so the revised sequence must represent the distinct case once rather than presenting the repetition as a new case.","Include at least one pair of inconsistent labels for the same underlying case material. The labels should be attributable to different source contexts and should not be safely collapsed into one fact without an explicit instruction.","Include a repeated opening or other clearly identifiable pacing problem and at least one unnecessarily long hold that the comments explicitly authorize changing.","Include at least one transition location where the comments explicitly authorize a revised transition."]},"review_comments.xlsx":{"semantic_content":["Include Leonie Vasquez's finite review comments, each with a stable comment identifier or otherwise unique locator, and make every requested action deterministic.","The comments must explicitly authorize the required sequence change, removal of the repeated occurrence, pacing trims, and transition edits. They must not authorize new case facts or invented connective narration.","For the conflicting labels, include an explicit instruction to preserve attribution or mark the conflict for confirmation rather than silently selecting one label.","For the ambiguous date, include enough source context to establish that one date string has more than one plausible interpretation and explicitly authorize retaining the literal representation while recording the ambiguity for confirmation.","Include case-record fields that support all factual text and ordering decisions in the gold. Ensure duplicate and inconsistent-label conditions are genuine source conditions, not merely formatting noise.","Place a single column containing mixed date or time representations: one representation must be unambiguous and another must be ambiguous in ordinary professional use, such as a slash-delimited date without an explicit locale alongside a clearly year-first representation. Do not add another mixed-format column.","Include one retired helper column with stale values that conflict with the authoritative sequence or timing information. The column must be identifiable as retired from its source context, but its values must not be needed to derive the correct output.","Include one residual formula error in a non-authoritative cell left by a previous analyst. The error must be ignored, must not be needed for any gold value, and must not be repeated elsewhere.","Do not seed additional standard defects such as missing required fields, extra formula errors, unexplained blank records, corrupted files, or unrelated out-of-scope rows."]}},"gold_transformation":["Parse the draft sequence, case records, and review comments.","Apply the comments as the complete authorized edit list: deduplicate the repeated case occurrence, implement the explicitly requested order, make the authorized trims and pause changes, and place the authorized transitions.","Preserve source-supported factual wording and preserve attribution for the inconsistent labels. Retain the ambiguous date representation without asserting an unsupported calendar interpretation, and record the issue for confirmation.","Ignore the retired helper column and the residual formula error when deriving sequence, timing, and content.","Produce one DOCX containing the revised timed asset plus a change log that maps every comment to its disposition, affected case or time range, and resulting change. Include an explicit note for unresolved or confirmation-required material.","Ensure the final timeline is mathematically consistent and that no source-only helper fields or spreadsheet error strings appear in the output."],"gold_derivation":{"method":"Use an offline reference script to extract the source facts and comments, apply the authorized edit mapping, calculate the revised sequence and timings from authoritative fields, and generate the DOCX. Use relational source comparisons rather than hard-coded answer values.","validation":["Verify every distinct source case reference appears exactly once in the revised sequence.","Verify every authorized comment has one matching change-log entry.","Verify all output factual claims trace to the sources or authorized comment text.","Verify ambiguous-date handling, conflict attribution, stale-helper exclusion, and formula-error exclusion.","Verify timing tolerances, timeline geometry, rendered readability, and error-token hygiene."]}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"primary_plus_appendix","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"ref_case_review_draft","filename":"case_review_draft.docx","purpose":"The current timed case-review draft, including the source case facts, segment content, timing information, and existing editorial structure.","required":true,"discovery":"Open this document first to understand the draft asset and its source wording."},{"artifact_id":"ref_review_comments","filename":"review_comments.xlsx","purpose":"Leonie Vasquez's review comments and the accompanying case-record material needed to identify the authorized editorial changes and preserve source-supported facts.","required":true,"discovery":"Use this workbook alongside the draft; its comments identify the requested revisions."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"del_revised_case_review","filename":"gildenhall_case_review_revised.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A revised timed case-review video production document representing the edited asset, with the revised sequence and an embedded change log.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file into the top level of the solver's starting working directory.","Use exactly the specified filename.","Include the revised timed sequence and the embedded change log in the same document.","Preserve source-supported facts and distinguish unresolved conflicts from confirmed content.","Do not add unsupported narration, facts, participants, outcomes, or source-only working fields."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"inspect_quality","work_product":"media_edit","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"supplied_source@v4","occupation":"audio_video_technicians","sector":"information","task_archetype":"supplied_source","estimated_professional_hours":3.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"reference_script","reviewer_policy":"Generate the reference solution by parsing the supplied source files and applying only the finite authorized edits in the review comments, then have an independent reviewer compare the rendered document against the source facts, timings, and comments.","minimum_reviewers":1,"known_limitations":["The deliverable is a text-office representation of a timed edited video asset; grading verifies editorial sequence, timing, wording, and change documentation rather than audible waveform quality."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:16:56+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:16:56+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:16:56+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:16:56+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/f7652a24ac1e64cf","declared_deliverables":["gildenhall_case_review_revised.docx"]};
